    "duplicate": "Same substantive claim already graded, with no independent defect or coverage gap.",
    "false_positive": "A confident material claim contradicted by the staged source or a relevant existing assertion, based on an unsupported assumed contract, or requiring an input outside the documented API. Name the counterevidence. Generic requests to add already-present exact protection are false positives only if they materially allege the protection is absent.",
    "out_of_scope": "A concern outside the neutral behavior domain. Still flag materially unsupported factual assertions when present, but do not turn legitimate unrelated defects into scope-bound accepted detections.",
    "unresolved": "A plausible conditional concern that cannot be decided from the bounded source, including absent dependency/plugin behavior or an explicitly unresolved contract. Never silently promote this to accepted or false positive."
